    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement for the query (pitavastatin) is present in the supplied records.",
    "L4 records concern other molecules (risperidone, atorvastatin, rosuvastatin, oxaprozin) and do not provide query-specific intestinal absorption, solubility, or permeability data.",
    "No query-specific data on first-pass metabolism, transporter-mediated disposition, or intestinal permeability are provided beyond physicochemical priors.",
    "The query is fully ionized at physiological pH (neutral fraction 0), which may limit passive permeability, but the impact is unknown and is not affirmative evidence for F < 20%."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high because the query is a statin with the same dihydroxyheptenoic acid side chain and 4-fluorophenyl motif as cerivastatin, whose absolute oral bioavailability was 60% (90% CI 51-70%); L3 oral-exposure records for related statins are consistent with oral absorption, and L4 provides no query-specific absorption or permeability evidence that would overturn this. Confidence remains moderate because no direct query-specific F measurement is available."
}

